#Variant descriptions
#Full Variants
variants.NORMAL.desc=The base GTNH experience without any changes. You cannot turn this off, why would you do that anyways? :P
variants.GARDEN_OF_GRIND.desc=A variant that makes one, singular change: removing all world gen, turning all dimensions into void. Good luck, and... well, I would say don't die, but you don't have much of a choice in the matter.
variants.DIMLOCKED.desc=As the name implies, this variant locks you to a specific dimension which you cannot leave. You will spawn and respawn in that dimension and have to deal with all the challenges that present themselves from not having access to the intended progression path. You can specify the dimension ID you want this variant to lock you to, some examples include the Nether (-1), the End (1) and Ross128B (64). A full list of dimension IDs can be found on the GTNH wiki. All Dimlocks outside of a dimension that has a required resource will have alternative sources for that resource, i.e. chaos shards if not in the End, Nether Air if not in the Nether, etc. 
variants.SKYBLOCK.desc=Garden of Grind, but with less emphasis on the grind. This variant provides an all void dims skyblock alternative to the base pack with proper tools for resource generation and progression, and a nice little starting island so you dont have to fall into the void 400 times. You even get a tree, hurray!

#Sub-Variants
variants.NO_RECIPE_ADDITIONS.desc=If you see this, something went wrong.
variants.VOID_WORLD.desc=The whole world is gone! All dimensions are made of pure nothingness, your spawn dimension included. Have fun embracing the void!
variants.VOID_ISLAND.desc=You're stranded on a small island floating in the void, with nothing but some basic items and a tree. But there's still hope, other dimensions seem to still be intact...
variants.NO_ROCKET.desc=One of the most popular challenge runs, No Rocket is what it says on the tin, all rockets are disabled. You'll have to find ways around all the space-exclusive resources you are missing out on. 
variants.NO_QUEST_REWARDS.desc=Rather self explanatory, you will not be able to receive aid from the quest gods, as all quest rewards are disabled.
variants.ALTERED_TIME.desc=Alter time with this variant, either lengthening or shortening all recipe times. The number you enter in the textbox is the multiplier that will be applied to recipes, use a number >1 if you want recipes to take longer, and <1 if you want them to be shorter. 0 makes all recipes 1 tick long.
variants.ALTERED_EFFICIENCY.desc=Alter the laws of energy conservation with this variant, either increasing or decreasing generator efficiencies across the board. The number you enter in the textbox is the multiplier that will be applied to generators, use a number >1 if you want generators to generate more power, and <1 if you want them to generate less.
variants.INFINITE_POWER.desc=INFINITE POWER! This variant fills your wireless network to a number so large that you will never be able to deplete it. Also, in order to be able to use that power, all energy hatches are now wireless! Rejoice in your wealth of unlimited energy!
variants.CUSTOM_DIM_START.desc=This variant allows you to choose a starting dimension in which you are going to spawn and respawn, but there is nothing preventing you from leaving. You can specify the dimension ID you want this variant to start you in, some examples include the Nether (-1), the End (1) and Ross128B (64). A full list of dimension IDs can be found on the GTNH wiki.
variants.SUPERFLAT.desc=4 layers thick flat terrain awaits you in this variant. All dimensions are now superflat, with each dimension having its own unique block layers. By default, this variant will disable all types of chunk population, meaning your world will be barren of foliage and structures, but you can enable this using the checkbox below. Similarly, all biomes are plains by default, unless biome diversity is enabled. Villages will always generate, regardless of the setting chosen.
variants.MONOBLOCK.desc=Monoblock meaning one block. THE one block your whole world will be made of. Terrain will generate as usual, but it will all be replaced by the one chosen block type. You can choose any block you wish by entering its identifier as follows: modID:blockname:meta . §4WARNING: This variant can cause performance issues and crashes depending on the block chosen.

